SI GAMES — changes.log
======================
Newest entry first. Markers: FIX = something broken, ADD = new thing,
CHG = behaviour changed, DEL = removed.

2026-10-26 — code health, colour themes, six new titles
-------------------------------------------------------

ADD  Colour themes (6 palettes, header switcher)
     The whole shell now paints from CSS custom properties instead of
     hardcoded hex: --si-accent*, --si-glow*, --si-bg, --si-panel* etc.
     A theme is only a re-declaration of those tokens on
     :root[data-theme="…"], so one rule set recolours cards, buttons,
     borders, the player, the boot screen and the launch pages.
       · Nebula  — neon blue / violet (the original palette, unchanged)
       · Plasma  — violet / hot pink
       · Crimson — red / amber
       · Tidal   — azure / aqua
       · Toxic   — green / lime
       · Solar   — orange / gold
     Switcher: src/components/ThemePicker.tsx (header, next to the status
     line). Logic: src/lib/themes.ts. Selection persists in localStorage
     under "si-games-theme" and is applied before first paint from
     main.tsx, so there is no flash of the wrong palette. The browser
     chrome (theme-color meta) follows the active theme, and the landing
     starfield re-tints itself too (--si-star-hot / --si-star-cool, plus a
     "si-theme-change" window event from applyTheme()).

ADD  Six new titles to the library (all verified reachable and served
     without X-Frame-Options / frame-ancestors, so they load in-frame):
       · Slither.io      — slither.io        (Arcade, .io)
       · Shell Shockers  — shellshock.io     (Shooter, FPS)
       · Surviv.io       — surviv.io         (Shooter, Battle Royale)
       · Sandspiel       — sandspiel.club    (Sandbox, falling sand)
       · Hextris         — hextris.github.io (Puzzle, stacking)
       · Skribbl.io      — skribbl.io        (Party, drawing)
     Each carries a description, a real control map and a generated star
     cover (no new remote image dependencies).

FIX  Header layout — the stylesheet has always targeted a
     `.site-header .header-inner` wrapper (the mobile breakpoint sets its
     width) but no such element existed, so brand, nav and status rendered
     as full-width blocks stacked flush against the viewport edge. The
     wrapper is back in Landing.tsx, laid out as a centred flex row on
     desktop (min(1120px, 100% - 40px), matching the main column) and
     keeping the existing mobile width rule working.

FIX  Lint went from 12 errors to 0 (`bun run lint` now exits clean; the
     remaining 21 warnings are the pre-existing react-refresh notices on
     template/vendor files):
       · Dashboard.tsx      — dropped unused CardDescription + Navigate
                              imports.
       · games.ts           — applyLibraryPatch destructured a `lead`
                              marker it never used (x2); replaced with an
                              explicit id/label/url/external projection.
       · Landing.tsx        — favorites/recent were read from localStorage
                              in a mount effect (setState-in-effect); they
                              are now lazy useState initialisers. The
                              "reset pagination when filters change"
                              effect became applyQuery / applyCategory /
                              applySortBy callbacks, so paging resets
                              exactly where the filter changes.
       · GamePlayer.tsx     — the [game] effect synchronised six pieces of
                              state on every title change. The player is
                              now keyed by resolvedId, so switching games
                              remounts it: all of that state is initial
                              state again, and the effect only records the
                              visit in "si-games-recent". Favorites also
                              moved to a lazy initialiser.
       · InstallerAd.tsx    — dismissal flag read from localStorage in an
                              effect → lazy initialiser; useEffect import
                              removed.
       · use-mobile.ts      — window.matchMedia + setState-in-effect →
                              useSyncExternalStore (subscribes properly,
                              no state sync in the body).
       · ui/carousel.tsx    — setApi and the first scroll-flag read were
                              synchronous setState in effect bodies; both
                              now hand over after the effect settles. The
                              "reInit" listener was registered but never
                              removed — cleanup now offs it too.
       · ui/sidebar.tsx     — SidebarMenuSkeleton called Math.random()
                              inside a useMemo during render; the width is
                              now picked once per instance in a lazy
                              useState initialiser.

CHG  src/index.css and src/player-prompt.css: every accent, glow, panel and
     surface hex (5608f8, 3efeff, 4320e0, 0d1527, 060e22, 131e36, 182645,
     1a2b55, 0a142e, 101a35, 1e2d55, 7ff9ff …) now resolves through a
     token, including the translucent variants (--si-accent-18 … -88,
     --si-glow-12 … -40). Neutral values (text greys, the yellow SI
     Installer block, dark overlays) were deliberately left alone.


Earlier sessions (recorded here after the fact)
-----------------------------------------------

· GTA V — the mode picker was removed from the main card; the title now
